{"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each OnboardingKit feature has its own views, like the flows in "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/Flows-Article","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":", the screen templates in ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/Screens-Article","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", the USP views in "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/USPs-Article"},{"type":"text","text":", and the “what’s new” views in "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/WhatsNew-Article","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"OnboardingKit also has feature-agnostic views, that aren’t tied to a certain feature. These views are used by the feature views, but can also be used as standalone views, to build your own onboarding screens."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"All views can be styled with view modifiers that apply a style to the environment. This means that you can apply a style to a parent view, and it will be used by all views within it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Page Content","anchor":"Page-Content","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/OnboardingPageContent","isActive":true},{"text":" can be used to wrap the content of an onboarding page. It centers the content and applies edge paddings and a max width, to make the page look good on all screen sizes:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["OnboardingPageContent {","    VStack {","        Image(systemName: \"hand.wave\")","        Text(\"Welcome!\")","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This view is used by screens like "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/OnboardingWelcomeScreen","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/OnboardingWhatsNewScreen","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", and is a good fit for custom pages in flows like "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/OnboardingPageFlow","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/OnboardingSlideshow","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The page content can be styled with an "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/OnboardingPageContentStyle"},{"type":"text","text":", which is applied with "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/SwiftUICore\/View\/onboardingPageContentStyle(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". It defines the max width and height of the content."}]},{"text":"Primary Button","anchor":"Primary-Button","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/OnboardingButton","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is a large, full-width button that can be used for the main actions of an onboarding, for instance at the bottom of a flow:"}]},{"code":["OnboardingButton(\"Continue\") {","    state.showNextPage(orDismiss: dismiss)","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"You can use an ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/OnboardingButtonType","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" to make the button "},{"code":".primary","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".secondary"},{"type":"text","text":", or to use a glass variant like "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".primaryGlass"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".secondaryGlass"},{"type":"text","text":". The glass variants only render as glass on platforms where the glass effect is available."}]},{"anchor":"Vertical-Progress-List","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Vertical Progress List"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/OnboardingVerticalProgressList","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" lists a set of "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/OnboardingVerticalProgressListStep","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" steps in a vertical list, where all steps up to the current step are highlighted:"}]},{"code":["OnboardingVerticalProgressList(","    steps: [","        .init(title: \"Create an account\", text: \"It only takes a minute.\"),","        .init(title: \"Add a friend\", text: \"Things are more fun together.\"),","        .init(title: \"Start sharing\", text: \"Share your first photo.\")","    ],","    stepIndex: 1",")"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The list can be styled with an "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/OnboardingVerticalProgressListStyle","isActive":true},{"text":", which is applied with ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/SwiftUICore\/View\/onboardingVerticalProgressListStyle(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". It defines the step spacing, as well as the size and colors of the step circles and titles."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Popovers","text":"Popovers"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"OnboardingKit has a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/SwiftUICore\/View\/onboardingPopover(_:isPresented:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" view modifier that can present a text popover from any view, and a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/SwiftUICore\/View\/onboardingPopover(isPresented:content:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" modifier that can present custom popover content."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["Button(\"Share\") { share() }","    .onboardingPopover(","        \"Tap here to share with your friends.\",","        isPresented: $isPopoverPresented","    )"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Popovers aren’t available on tvOS and watchOS."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Features","title":"Features","identifiers":["doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/Pages-Article","doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/Flows-Article","doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/Screens-Article","doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/USPs-Article","doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/WhatsNew-Article"]}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit"]]},"metadata":{"title":"Views","modules":[{"name":"OnboardingKit"}],"roleHeading":"API Collection","role":"collectionGroup"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"text":"This article describes the OnboardingKit views.","type":"text"}],"topicSections"